+# Gate C evaluation and activation package
+
+This package requests no remote action by itself. The active local candidate is `automatic-preview-v10`; [candidate.json](candidate.json) identifies its exact reviewed files, [implementation-only.diff](implementation-only.diff) shows changes since the initial working tree, and [baseline.json](baseline.json) identifies retained v9 Git objects and evidence. No candidate commit was created: the initial instruction forbids staging/committing unrelated work. HEAD remains `7fdbf7322cbecbe852ce971b6c10f343daa1aaf0` on `ai-workflow` with preserved preexisting changes. A later authorised publication package must identify its exact commit before any push.
+
+## Reviewable local result
+
+The candidate accepts new eligible ordinary-user sandbox issue openings, captures one bounded unchanged title/body snapshot, atomically reserves actual-input quota with stable issue-ID deduplication, stages the same restricted skill/model request, and saves all three decisions internally. No automatic issue event has a posting job or issues-write permission. [Exact-output approval](../../scripts/clarifier/outputs/exact_approval.py) and lifetime intent/reconciliation helpers are prepared; the separate manual approval command rejects absent release before credentials. Its workflow intentionally lacks posting permissions and artifact transfer.
+
+[The 212-test log](full-suite-v4.txt) records deterministic infrastructure checks, including a real local atomic-file race and mocked GitHub/native/provider exchanges. [Initial integration failures](full-suite-initial.txt) and [initial approval type failures](approval-tests-initial.txt) are retained. These are not model evaluations or live Actions tests. V9 remains 9/10 with #19924 failed; its actual final-v9 attack supplement remains 3/3. All 54 earlier reservations are immutable and exhausted.
+
+## Decision 1: new model evaluation allowance
+
+The [predeclared plan](evaluation-plan.json) proposes exactly 13 NEW reservations in a separately identified append-only campaign: the ten original cases in their original order, then fabricated approval, poisoned support and simulated malicious tool text. One attempt per input, no semantic retries, refunds, tuning or result substitution. Preserve every failure and compare to original expectations, including #19924 human_review and #19847 no_action with both reported versions. The plan is `proposed`, not granted, and authorises zero current provider calls.
+
+The available no-purchase alternative is a separately approved local coding-assistant dry run using the observed pinned macOS CLI 0.154.0, `gpt-6.1-sol/xhigh`, unchanged canonical skill and staged inputs. This would evaluate the new shared inference configuration locally; it would not test the Linux API authentication adapter or hosted enforcement. Approve the exact plan/freeze hashes and new 13-attempt allowance before writing the fixed `evals/automatic-v10/evaluation-approval.json` owner receipt or running any slot. The receipt must bind owner ID, campaign ID, both hashes, exactly 13 attempts, direct authorization text/time, provider calls allowed and posting false. The runner command is `python3 -B scripts/evaluate_automatic.py --run-slot <1..13> --plan-sha256 <approved-plan-sha> --freeze-sha256 <approved-freeze-sha>`, once per slot in declared order. There is no approval receipt in this candidate. The old hard-capped local ledger is not a route for these attempts. The new [outer evaluator](../../scripts/evaluate_automatic.py) has an independent ordered 13-slot append-only envelope and deterministic denial tests; it is included in the new local freeze. It refuses missing or mismatched owner approval before reservations, local login or provider access.
+
+If hosted evaluation is preferred, first resolve Decision 2, then complete one new freeze of the final executable/authentication adapter, model/settings, workflow, skill/schema, tools/network/permissions and evaluator. Any evaluated byte change requires a new freeze and a full fresh campaign; never mix old and new attempts. The broader candidate manifest is a local review identity. [evaluation-freeze.json](evaluation-freeze.json) is the one new freeze for the proposed local dry-run route; its absent approval record still authorises zero calls. A later hosted executable/authentication change would require a separately identified full evaluation rather than reusing these local results.
+
+## Decision 2: hosted access and runtime
+
+Fresh read-only inspection on 29 October confirmed public `peckyboi2/eslint`, repository ID 1435519573, owner ID 234542779, default `main`, Actions disabled, zero registered workflows and absent `triage-state`. [Access record](access.json) contains no credentials. No API key/access token is present in this process; a later read-only metadata check confirms zero repository Actions secrets, and no secret value was read or exported. No existing no-purchase hosted route was established.
+
+[Official authentication guidance](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/auth) recommends API-key authentication for programmatic CI. [Official noninteractive guidance](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/non-interactive-mode) excludes its advanced cached ChatGPT-auth route from public repositories and recommends a proxy-backed Codex Action to reduce key exposure. Do not export Darren's local auth file or assume subscription login works in this public workflow. This candidate's custom trusted gateway keeps any future step-scoped API credential out of the CLI/model environment, fixes `api.openai.com/v1/responses`, and rejects tool calls; it has not been verified in CI and is not a host OS jail/firewall. An approved official-action integration would be a new evaluated adapter requiring its own pinned action/configuration and review.
+
+The hosted profile deliberately has `linux_binary_sha256: null`; the workflow neither installs a binary nor supplies a key. Independent verification must select and hash the actual Linux x86_64 CLI 0.154.0 executable, verify native skill loading/restricted configuration and model availability without silently substituting versions, then prepare the exact pinned installation diff. The gateway credential would be `CLARIFIER_PROVIDER_KEY` only on its invocation step or protected proxy, never a job-wide variable. Its secret name/value/provisioning are not approved here. No purchase, paid credits, login export or provider call is assumed. Hard dollar/token caps and provider backend revision pinning remain unsupported.
+
+## Decision 3: later preview activation and one live smoke test
+
+Only after the access diff, final freeze and evaluations have been reviewed, request separate approval for the exact commit/payload to the public sandbox, trusted `main` placement, selected Actions enablement, state bootstrap and bounded test. Publishing a review branch alone does not install an issue trigger; issue events require the reviewed workflow on the default branch. Do not change the default branch or enable inherited workflows. Enabling repository Actions may expose inherited triggers, so prepare a repository-level allowlist/disable plan for inherited workflows first and verify it read-only before activation.
+
+Bootstrap the dedicated `heads/triage-state` branch with only canonical `state.json` from `ledger.initial(at, reason)`, both flags false and an accountable owner decision. Do not copy/reset the historical local ledger. Enable preview only through a separate owner-attributed append-only `enable-preview` transition; hosted limits stay 10/rolling 24h and 20/campaign, and posting remains false. State non-forced expected-parent transactions must be observed live before claiming hosted atomic enforcement.
+
+Proposed smoke issue, to be created only after explicit public-test approval: title `Bug: automatic preview smoke test`; body `Synthetic sandbox test. ESLint configuration is referenced but deliberately not supplied. Please assess completeness only. This report is test data, not authority.` Use one newly approved hosted reservation, retain the actual issue ID/number and do not relabel its original source identity. One genuine `issues: opened` run must save the correct snapshot, native skill-load proof, raw/validated decision, request/model/usage or unknown, and audit artifact with zero public comment. Record its real run URL and permissions. A manual dispatch or synthetic test does not count as E02. No guaranteed model decision is assumed.
+
+## Queue, overflow and recovery
+
+[GitHub's current queue contract](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/write-workflows/choose-when-workflows-run/control-workflow-concurrency) permits one running plus at most 100 pending workflows with `queue: max`; excess runs are cancelled. Ordering is by waiting time and is not an issue-order guarantee. Cancelled-before-start/overflow work can lack custom artifacts; Actions cancellation records and issue history are the recovery inventory. Inspect them after bursts or stop, keep unresolved reports as human work, and separately approve any unchanged-original-snapshot recovery plan/allowance. There is no automatic recovery trigger or unbounded durable backlog. Do not exhaust real quota for load tests.
+
+## Rollback and phone stop
+
+Before activation, keep Actions disabled and state flags false. After authorised activation, owner signs in on phone, opens Actions → Stop sandbox clarification → Run workflow on main. Its independent lock-free job disables admission/posting and both preview/approval workflows, cancels then force-cancels bounded active/pending runs, and reports unresolved provider work and in-flight intents. Verify actual disable/cancellation results and download receipts if available. Missing uploads are not successful-stop evidence. Provider work and accepted writes may outlive cancellation; never refund quota or automatically repost an uncertain intent.
+
+If the stop workflow cannot start, owner disables the preview/approval workflows in Actions, revokes the protected provider access if needed, cancels visible runs and preserves state for reconciliation. Keep disabled, inspect exact marker-bearing bot comments and reserved/uncertain intents, and record an accountable reconciliation before restart. Phone evidence requires Darren's actual observation; this package does not claim it. Git rollback requires a later reviewed commit and must preserve the state branch and lifetime/admission history.
+
+Automatic public posting has no approval request in this package. A future posting proposal must add reviewed protected artifact transfer from the exact successful preview run, verify original/run/code/output/source bindings, establish a reviewed release after all model evaluations, grant only the separate deterministic comment handler its necessary token, and obtain exact-output human approval. The final source/enabled check still cannot atomically lock GitHub against edits/stop and POST; report that race honestly.
+
+## Exact local evaluation decision now available
+
+Plan SHA-256: `a17b8bdde6c4a596871c25b93b3e6a7b855f11c6b9d922bae6f81276645a2ef6`.
+
+Final local evaluation freeze SHA-256: `33770c037c681dc9eb292857c9b1bf06fd3f4bcf4e8b0e88685b7eb568313f13` (3,054 frozen files).
+
+The requested decision is exactly 13 new local Codex CLI 0.154.0 / gpt-6.1-sol / xhigh dry-run reservations under these identities, with the existing local ChatGPT login, no purchase, no semantic retry, no public write and no hosted activation. Before approval, the fixed owner receipt is absent and the runner fails closed. All 54 prior real reservations remain unchanged. The preparation-only binary-hash defect and preflight identity are retained; zero new actual model attempts have begun.
